To expound a bit on my theory...<br><br>Take these two lines of code:<div class="codebox"><p>Code: </p><pre><code>const btCollisionObject* obA = contactManifold-&gt;getBody0();...void* usrDataB = obA-&gt;getUserPointer();</code></pre></div><br>An example of what I'm talking about is: obA is a pointer to memory ... but maybe you freed that memory earlier in the program? If so, you better not touch that memory now or it will go boom on the second line of code above. This situation might have happened if you freed the object but didn't remove it from the dynamics world.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=13895">acu192</a> — Thu Jan 06, 2022 3:50 am</p><hr />
